{
	title: 'Background jobs show in the activity words and the tab marker',
	spec: 'While background Bash jobs run, the activity words in the terminal prompt rule and the web status line name them: "2 background jobs" when nothing else happens, else after the activity ("writing · 2 jobs"). The tab marker shows them in bash magenta (colors.tab jobsFg, CSS --jobs-fg): a working tab\'s ▪ alternates between its color and magenta every other blink; an idle tab with jobs blinks a magenta ▪ (mark kind jobs, ranked with working). The Hal cursor is unchanged. Terminal and web match. Tab.jobs counts meta.background; the host broadcasts session meta whenever meta.background changes, which republishes tabs.',
